<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">14 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 14 November, from 565 to 1969.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">565 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,461 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Emperor Justinian I dies</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Justinian died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> after a 38-year reign. He reconquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, codified <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-law">Roman law</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corpus-juris-civilis">Corpus Juris Civilis</a> and built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia">Hagia Sophia</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corpus-juris-civilis">Corpus Juris Civilis</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia">Hagia Sophia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justinian-i">Justinian I</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1770">1770 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">256 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">James Bruce reaches what he believes is the source of the Nile</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Scottish traveller <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-bruce">James Bruce</a> reached Gish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blue-nile">Abay</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>, the source of the Lesser Abay, and celebrated with toasts. Admitting that the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-nile">White Nile</a> was longer, he argued that the Blue <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> was the Nile of the ancients.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-bruce">James Bruce</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1812">1812 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">214 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Wittgenstein's Russians defeat Victor and Oudinot at Smoliani</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Russians under General Peter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ludwig-wittgenstein">Wittgenstein</a> defeated the French forces of Marshal Claude Victor and Marshal Nicholas Oudinot at Smoliani. It was the last French effort to re-establish their northern flank in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, the Dvina Line.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleonic-wars">Napoleonic Wars</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/london" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/london.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1851">1851 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">175 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Moby-Dick is published in New York</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Harper and Brothers published Herman Melville's Moby-Dick, a month after its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> edition. Poorly received at first, the tale of Captain <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahab">Ahab</a>'s pursuit of the white whale is now a classic of American literature.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1889">1889 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">137 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nellie Bly sets out to beat Phileas Fogg's 80 days</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> World reporter Nellie Bly left Hoboken to travel around the world faster than Jules Verne's fictional hero. She returned in just over 72 days, a world record at the time.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1940">1940 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">86 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Luftwaffe devastates Coventry</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Some 500 German bombers attacked Coventry overnight, killing about 570 people and destroying the medieval cathedral. It was one of the heaviest raids of the Blitz.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1965">1965 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">61 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Battle of Ia Drang begins in Vietnam's central highlands</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The first major battle between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> Army and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-army-of-vietnam">People's Army of Vietnam</a> began at the foot of the Chu Pong Massif. It saw the first large-scale helicopter air assault and the first tactical use of B-52 bombers.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam-war">Vietnam War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1969">1969 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">57 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Apollo 12 launches for the Moon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apollo">Apollo</a> 12 survived two lightning strikes during launch from Cape Kennedy. Five days later Pete Conrad and Alan Bean landed precisely beside the Surveyor 3 probe in the Ocean of Storms.</p></div></li></ol>
